  title: 'Housing in Singapore (Present Day) '
  info: "Singapore offers a mix of public and private housing, with over 80% of residents
    living in HDB flats. These government-subsidized apartments provide affordable
    homeownership options. Private condominiums and landed properties cater to higher-income
    groups. Rental costs vary by location, with central areas being the most expensive.
    The government implements strict housing policies to ensure sustainability, including
    property cooling measures and foreign ownership restrictions. Despite limited
    land, Singapore\u2019s urban planning prioritizes efficiency, greenery, and accessibility,
    making housing an essential aspect of daily life.  "
  image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 88baf38a697df4a01a0ace0cf81a7f9e, type: 3}
